{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:23-2","provision":"BCO 23-2","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"23-2","title":"Section 23-2","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/23-2/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/23-2","current_text":{"html":"<p>The Presbytery may designate a minister as honorably retired when the minister by reason of age wishes to be retired, or as medically disabled when by reason of infirmity is no longer able to serve the church in the active ministry of the Gospel. A minister medically disabled or honorably retired shall continue to hold membership in his Presbytery. He may serve on committees or commissions if so elected or appointed.</p>","text":"The Presbytery may designate a minister as honorably retired when the minister by reason of age wishes to be retired, or as medically disabled when by reason of infirmity is no longer able to serve the church in the active ministry of the Gospel. A minister medically disabled or honorably retired shall continue to hold membership in his Presbytery. He may serve on committees or commissions if so elected or appointed."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:23","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Reco